CONCEPT: The PARTITION loop invariant divides A[p..r] into four regions: values known to be ≤ x, values known to be > x, values not yet examined, and the pivot x at A[r].
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): At every moment before the final pivot placement, i and j are not arbitrary indices: they are the boundaries separating ≤ x, > x, and unrestricted regions.
